  "result": "The test checks that the Courses card header (found by its positional selector, outside any iframe) still has `background-color` `rgb(13, 110, 253)`, the value from the before snapshot. It passes on the before snapshot. It fails on the after snapshot with an assertion that names the selector and gives the expected and actual colors (`rgb(108, 117, 125)` is gray).\n\nThere's a conflict you should know about. The design intent says the PR was meant to change \"the padding and the background color\". The diff confirms both: `mb-4` became `mb-2`, and `bg-primary` became `bg-secondary` in `StudentCoursesCard.tsx`. So the only flagged box is a change the PR meant to make. Rule 4 says not to assert on intended changes, but the test also has to fail on the after snapshot. Nothing else in the diff or the flagged boxes differs, so the background color is the only thing it could check. That makes this flag most likely a false positive rather than a real regression.",
